  "id": "sensory",
  "term": "sensory",
  "definition": "Sensory refers to how a person takes in and makes sense of signals from inside the body and from the surrounding environment so they can respond effectively. When this functioning is altered, it can interfere with regulating, combining, or telling apart sensory information and may reduce daily functioning, participation, and well-being.",
